archmage84 wrote:
> I've lost two decent files now, through no fault other than my
> computer being weird. Thus, I'm considering making regular backups. Is
> it looked down upon to make backups of files, if you make sure you
> don't savescum? How many of you do it?
> 
> archmage84

As long as you don't use the backup to recover from a mistake, you're
fine.  Just don't use the backup at all unless the game crashes and
recover doesn't work.  As a general guideline, if you can admit to
everything backup-related you did in your YA(F)AP, your conscience is
probably clear.  After all, it's less save-scumming itself that's
wrong so much as it is claiming such games as legitimate ascensions.

I don't think I kept a backup during my first ascension, due to the
same sort of paranoia about savescumming that you're showing, but
after that I started keeping backups a bit more often.  After
this <http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/
browse_thread/thread/fded17ed754839f5/> happened, I've made a
point of frequently backing up any promising games; I don't want
to come that close to losing an ascension over something that isn't
at all related to the game itself again.


